.SH "5\&.0\&.0"
.PP
.SS "Breaking changes"
.SS "\fRconstructor\fP equality now required"
To align with other implementations common in the community, but also to be more functionally correct, the two objects being compared now must have equal \fRconstructor\fPs\&.
.SS "\fRMap\fP / \fRSet\fP comparisons no longer support IE11"
In previous verisons, \fR\&.forEach()\fP was used to ensure that support for \fRSymbol\fP was not required, as IE11 did not have \fRSymbol\fP and therefore both \fRMap\fP and \fRSet\fP did not have iterator-based methods such as \fR\&.values()\fP or \fR\&.entries()\fP\&. Since IE11 is no longer a supported browser, and support for those methods is present in all browsers and Node for quite a while, the comparison has moved to use these methods\&. This results in a ~20% performance increase\&.
.SS "\fRcreateCustomEqual\fP contract has changed"
To better facilitate strict comparisons, but also to allow for \fRmeta\fP use separate from caching, the contract for \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP has changed\&. See the \fRREADME documentation\fP for more details, but froma high-level:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRmeta\fP is no longer passed through to equality comparators, but rather a general \fRstate\fP object which contains \fRmeta\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRcache\fP now also lives on the \fRstate\fP object, which allows for use of the \fRmeta\fP property separate from but in parallel with the circular cache
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRequals\fP is now on \fRstate\fP, which prevents the need to pass through the separate \fRisEqual\fP method for the equality comparator
.PP
.SS "\fRcreateCustomCircularEqual\fP has been removed"
You can create a custom circular equality comparator through \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP now by providing \fRcircular: true\fP to the options\&.
.SS "Custom \fRmeta\fP values are no longer passed at callsite"
To use \fRmeta\fP properties for comparisons, they must be returned in a \fRcreateState\fP method\&.
.SS "Deep links have changed"
If you were deep-linking into a specific asset type (ESM / CJS / UMD), they have changed location\&.

.PP
\fBNOTE\fP: You may no longer need to deep-link, as \fBthe build resolution has improved\fP\&.
.SS "Enhancements"
.SS "New "strict" comparators available"
The following new comparators are available:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstrictDeepEqual\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstrictShallowEqual\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstrictCircularDeepEqual\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstrictCircularShallowEqual\fP
.PP

.PP
This will perform the same comparisons as their non-strict counterparts, but will verify additional properties (non-enumerable properties on objects, keyed objects on \fRArray\fP / \fRMap\fP / \fRSet\fP) and that the descriptors for the properties align\&.
.SS "\fRTypedArray\fP support"
Support for comparing all typed array values is now supported, and you can provide a custom comparator via the new \fRareTypedArraysEqual\fP option in the \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP configuration\&.
.SS "Better build system resolution"
The library now leverages the \fRexports\fP property in the \fRpackage\&.json\fP to provide builds specific to your method of consumption (ESM / CommonJS / UMD)\&. There is still a minified UMD version available if you want to use it instead\&.
.SS "\fRarePrimitiveWrappersEqual\fP option added to \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP configuration"
If you want a custom comparator for primitive wrappers (\fRnew Boolean()\fP / \fRnew Number()\fP / \fRnew String()\fP) it is now available\&.
