.SS "Breaking Changes"
.SS "Certain ES2015 features are now required"
In previous versions, there were automatic fallbacks for certain ES2015 features if they did not exist:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fRRegExp\&.prototype\&.flags\fP\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fRWeakMap\fP\fP
.PP

.PP
Due to the omnipresence of support in both browser and NodeJS, these have been deprecated\&. There is still an option if you require support for these legacy environments, however; see \fR\fRcreateCustomEqual\fP\fP and \fR\fRcreateCustomCircularEqual\fP\fP for more details\&.
.SS "\fRcreateCustomEqual\fP contract has changed"
To allow more flexibility and customizability for a variety of edge cases, \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP now allows override of specific type value comparisons in addition to the general comparator it did prior\&. See \fRthe documentation\fP for more details\&.
.SS "Enhancements"
.SS "\fRcreateCustomCircularEqual\fP added"
Like \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP, it will create a custom equality comparator, with the exception that it will handle circular references\&. See \fRthe documentation\fP for more details\&.
.SS "Cross-realm comparisons are now supported"
Prior to \fR4\&.x\&.x\&.\fP, \fRinstanceof\fP was used internally for checking of object classes, which only worked when comparing objects from the same \fRRealm\fP\&. This has changed to instead use an object's \fRStringTag\fP, which is not realm-specific\&.
.SS "TypeScript typings improved"
For better typing in edge-case scenarios like custom comparators with \fRmeta\fP values, typings have been refactored for accuracy and better narrow flow-through\&.
