.SS "Breaking changes"
When creating a custom equality comparator via \fRcreateCustomEqual\fP, the equality method has an expanded contract:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Before
type EqualityComparator = (objectA: any, objectB: any, meta: any) => boolean;

// After
type InternalEqualityComparator = (
  objectA: any,
  objectB: any,
  indexOrKeyA: any,
  indexOrKeyB: any,
  parentA: any,
  parentB: any,
  meta: any,
) => boolean;
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you have a custom equality comparator, you can ignore the differences by just passing additional \fRundefined\fP parameters, or you can use the parameters to further improve / clarify the logic\&.

